stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Prepared: explicit primary/follower, before key
    Prepared --> Prepared: no key, original retained
    Prepared --> Candidate: durable AnyKey, same O capture
    Candidate --> Result: exact ticket and current actor admission
    Result --> Pending: row unreadable/changed before release, lease kept
    Result --> Released: exact actor / nonce / cutoff CAS
    Result --> Transferred: durable result, no own lease, successor row proven
    Result --> TransferUnreadable: no own lease, row proof unreadable
    TransferUnreadable --> Result: repair proof, retain successor and debt
    Transferred --> Neutral: exact key/actor ledger settled, no successor mutation
    Neutral --> [*]: no row delete or wake
    Released --> Pending: row unreadable / changed / CAS miss
    Pending --> Released: repair and resubmit same durable result
    Released --> RowGone: exact snapshot CAS or proven absence
    RowGone --> Admitted: outcome + notice ack + cleanup CAS
    Admitted --> Wake: primary first cleanup only
    Admitted --> [*]: follower, parent unchanged
    Wake --> [*]

    state "Boot custody consumer (OFF)" as BootConsumer {
        [*] --> BootPrepare
        BootPrepare --> BootHeld: unreadable / conflicting full record
        BootHeld --> BootPrepare: actual artifact repaired
        BootPrepare --> BootAdopted: full registration + saved proof validated
        BootAdopted --> BootReaped: existing custody prepare then reaper
        BootReaped --> BootPending: outcome absent (no fabrication)
        BootPending --> BootPending: generic terminal / GC preserves unsettled debt
        BootReaped --> BootRegistered: saved outcome / actor-local barrier
        BootRegistered --> BootSettle: notice enqueue outside actor
        BootSettle --> BootHeld: exact authority or terminal custody failed
        BootSettle --> BootConsumed: old-row CAS or debt-only transfer
        BootConsumed --> BootOwnerDrive: existing recover / admission ready
    }
